I'm telling you this plainly instead of pretending it's done.

What I *can* do: hand you this ready-to-run folder, already tested
working with real login protection, so setting it up takes you a few
minutes, not hours. Free options that run a Node app like this one
persistently, with no credit card:

- **Render** (free web service tier) — connect a GitHub repo, it detects
  `node server.js`, add `CHAIRMAN_USER`/`CHAIRMAN_PASS` as environment
  variables in their dashboard (never commit your password to the repo),
  deploy. Free tier sleeps after inactivity and wakes on the next visit.
- **Railway** (free trial credit, no card for the trial) — same flow:
  push this folder to a GitHub repo, import it, set the two env vars,
  deploy.
- **Fly.io** (free allowance) — a bit more setup (their CLI + a small
  config file) but runs full-time without sleeping.
- **Replit** — paste this code into a Node repl, set the env vars as
  "Secrets," click Run; simplest if you don't want to touch GitHub at
  all, but the free tier's address can change and it sleeps when idle.

Any of these gets you a real `https://` address, gated by the login this
